    "summary": "Epic Dark Star > Stella Blue > Eyes sequence, tight playing throughout",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a monumental Dark Star that morphs into Stella Blue and flows into Eyes Of The World, highlighted by soaring Here Comes Sunshine and a jazzy Weather Report Suite. Jerry’s cosmic guitar work intertwines with Phil’s booming bass, while the rhythm section stays locked in. The audience recording captures the 23‑song marathon with remarkable clarity.",
    "review": "On October 30, 1973 at Kiel Auditorium the Dead turned a regular night into a historic marathon. Kicking off with a bright Here Comes Sunshine, the first set built momentum through classics like Jack Straw and a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, ending on a rousing Playing In The Band. The second set is where the magic truly unfolds: Dark Star stretches to 28 minutes before melting into an inspired Stella Blue and then soaring into Eyes Of The World, all underpinned by Phil’s thunderous bass and Jerry’s lyrical, cosmic leads. A Weather Report Suite that glides from Prelude through Part 1 into Let It Grow adds a jazzy, big‑band texture courtesy of Keith’s organ, while the rhythm section holds everything together with solid grooves. The audience recording is praised as one of the best‑sounding 70s crowd tapes, delivering an immersive experience that lets listeners feel every nuance of this monumental night.",
